Implement user story SKY-002-a: Implement SkyscannerClient class and interfaces

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.ts with the SkyscannerClient class, SearchParams/FlightResult interfaces, global-fetch-based searchFlights, error handling, and mock mode logic.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/skyscanner/client.ts exports a SkyscannerClient class with constructor({ apiKey?: string }); apiKey is stored as a private field (# or private) and is not publicly readable
- SearchParams interface is exported with exactly: origin: string, destination: string, date: string, adults?: number
- FlightResult interface is exported with exactly: price: number, currency: string, airline: string, departure: string, arrival: string, duration: number, stops: number
- searchFlights uses the Node.js global fetch exclusively — no axios, node-fetch, or other HTTP dependency imported
- When no apiKey is passed and RAPIDAPI_KEY is unset, or when apiKey is an empty string, or when RAPIDAPI_KEY is set to an empty string with no constructor apiKey — SkyscannerClient throws an Error whose message references the missing key
- When an apiKey is provided to the constructor and RAPIDAPI_KEY is also set, the constructor-provided apiKey takes precedence
- When the API returns 4xx/5xx, searchFlights rejects with an Error including the HTTP status code; the apiKey value must not appear anywhere in the error message
- When the API response body is malformed or missing expected fields, searchFlights rejects with a descriptive parse/validation Error
- When MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API equals exactly 'true', searchFlights resolves with a deterministic, non-empty FlightResult[] fixture (≥2 results, valid shape, varying prices for SKY-004 cheapest-selection) and does not call fetch
- When MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API is unset, empty, or any value other than exact 'true' (e.g. 'false', '1', 'TRUE'), searchFlights performs the real fetch call — mock mode is strict opt-in, not a fuzzy truthy check
- Real HTTP/API failures (4xx, 5xx, network error, malformed body) are NEVER silently replaced with mock/fixture data — mock mode activates only via explicit MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true'
- tsc --noEmit exits 0 with no type errors





